+
+## `publishDirectoryNoReplace`
+
+Publish a complete, already prepared sibling directory under a new name on Linux or macOS. The caller must persist its exact `dev`/`ino` identity before calling. This operation never replaces an existing target, including an empty directory. It requires the native helper and a real, unchanged parent directory. The caller owns preparation and any later cleanup.
+
+```ts
+import { publishDirectoryNoReplace } from "@openclaw/fs-safe/atomic";
+
+const staged = await fs.lstat(stagedDir, { bigint: true });
+const receipt = publishDirectoryNoReplace({
+  stagedDir,
+  targetDir,
+  expectedIdentity: { dev: staged.dev, ino: staged.ino },
+  assertBeforeMutation: () => assertCurrentAuthority(),
+});
+```
+
+The native no-replace rename uses a retained parent descriptor. The helper checks the staged directory's identity before dispatch, checks the final name afterward, and syncs the parent. If verification or sync fails after rename, the error includes `details.publication: "published"`; reconcile the exact target before retrying. A concurrent same-privilege actor can replace the staged basename between the identity check and POSIX rename, so protect the private staging parent from unrelated writers. This API does not create, mark, remove, or infer ownership of directories.
